  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 112 PM EDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\nA mid/upper ridge over the area today will slowly shift east\ntonight, bringing increasing high clouds ahead of a shortwave\ntrough over the Plains. Some light precip with this trough will\nenter our southwest counties late Saturday night to early Sunday\nmorning. Moistening of the column will be from the top down, but\nmost of the area will maintain a dry layer beneath ~700 mb. Only\nthe southern Plateau and southern Valley are expected to see any\nmeasurable precip on Sunday (only a couple hundredths), with only\nvirga or a few sprinkles elsewhere. \n\nAn increasingly amplified pattern develops early next week, with a\nridge east of the MS River and a deep trough over the Plains. This\nwill provide dry and mild weather for Monday and Tuesday, with\nrain chances returning Wednesday as the trough shifts east of the\nMS River. This has the potential to be a dynamic system, as it\ndevelops a negative tilt and favorable upper jet positioning to\nenhance QG forcing. A couple possible impacts to watch for with \nthis system may be mountain wave winds, possibly starting Tuesday \nnight, and a QLCS along the cold front Wednesday/Wednesday night \n(instability will be a limiting factor for the severe potential). \nAt the least, it could bring some beneficial rainfall to help \nmitigate the drought conditions. Confidence this far out remains\ntoo low to highlight any specific impacts in the HWO, but the \nwording will be changed to \"low probability\".",
